text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text I stare straight up at the ceiling.
text In the darkness, I imagine the spot where the new family restaurant will open.
music BGM01.mp3
text I know the place well.
text When I was a student, I passed it every day on my way to school.
text So they're building a family restaurant in that deserted spot.
text Actually, if it's opening next month, it must already be there.
text I just hadn't known about it because it's been so long since I passed by.
text That's why I can't even imagine there being a family restaurant in that spot.
text The shape of the town keeps changing.
text And it's people like us that change it.
text For our own sakes.
text Part of that responsibility rests with me too.
text I don't know whether it's a good thing or a bad thing.
text It's not as if I particularly love plants or animals or forests...
text But the town I hold in my memories keeps changing.
text For some reason, I just can't accept that.
