text I feel calm now. Ehehe.
text She laughs as she pushes her shoulder against mine.
text She's changing too, from those days when she was weak.
text Maybe I'm the one who's afraid now.
text Maybe I'm the one who's standing still at the bottom of that hill now.
text Maybe I'm looking up in fear of a distant, uncertain future.
text I wrap my arms under Nagisa's neck and hold her tightly.
text I press my nose into her nape.
text @[Tomoya]
text Hey, Nagisa...
sound O27.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text Yes...?
text ...Always be by my side, watching over me...
text I want to articulate that to her, but I can't.
text For some reason, the words just don't come out.
text It feels as though if I say them, my wish will be washed away by some irresistible, overwhelming force.
text So instead, I kiss her on the neck.
text I wish that by doing this, I could tie both me and Nagisa to this spot.
text This room in this old apartment.
